  "Question": "If \\(|x - 2| = p,\\) where \\(x \\lt 2,\\) then \\(x - p =\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(2 - 2p\\)",
    "D": "\\(2p - 2\\)",
    "E": "\\(|2p - 2|\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Because \\(x<2\\), the expression \\(x-2\\) is negative. Its absolute value is therefore its opposite:\n\\[\np=|x-2|=-(x-2)=2-x.\n\\]\nRearranging gives \\(x=2-p\\), so\n\\[\nx-p=(2-p)-p=\\boxed{2-2p}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
